.TH ARC-SBS-GUI 1 "2026-10-21" "de-xr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
arc\-sbs\-gui \- graphical front end for Arc SBS conversion
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
arc\-sbs\-gui
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Launch the default FLTK 1.4.5 video conversion form and its isolated Python
worker. Build arc-sbs-fltk separately against the patched toolkit. The Python
wheel alone does not supply this executable. A prepared depth model and the
same backend dependencies as the command-line converter are required.
.PP
The native form provides file/model selection, compute and encoder choices,
half/full SBS, strength, convergence, eye order, overwrite confirmation,
progress, worker logs and cancellation. More options contains frame limits,
processing quality and device overrides. The first positional filename and
Qt drag-and-drop behavior are not implemented by the FLTK form.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DE_XR_TOOLKIT
Defaults to FLTK. Set exactly Qt6 to select the retained Python Qt frontend;
install the qt6 extra for that alternative. The gui extra is empty.
.TP
.B ARC_SBS_FLTK_BINARY
Override the native executable. Otherwise use build-fltk/arc-sbs-fltk in the
source checkout, then arc-sbs-fltk on PATH.
.TP
.B DE_XR_FLTK_PREFIX
Select the native shared-toolkit prefix. The Python wrapper adds its lib
directory to LD_LIBRARY_PATH.
.TP
.B ARC_SBS_MODEL
Override the default depth model. Keep its companion weights and provenance.
.SH FILES
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/arc-sbs/fltk.json stores native preferences, defaulting to
~/.config/arc-sbs/fltk.json. The optional Qt frontend uses separate Qt settings.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
uv run arc-sbs-gui
DE_XR_TOOLKIT=Qt6 uv run --extra qt6 arc-sbs-gui
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
arc\-sbs(1), qimgvr(1)
